[Music]  hello and welcome to playstation grenade  remember when there were so many games  released in february and march that we  didn't know what to play first well  april is nothing near those heights so  this may be a good month to catch up on  those older games that said there is a  handful of games and a few free ones too  which dropped late last month which you  should be aware of so let's do this  first up is lego star wars the skywalker  saga all nine entries of the mainline  movies are recreated in their lego  likenesses the other star wars spin-off  movies will be added over time as dlc  right away there's over 300 characters  from the series to be collected and used  the game is set with each trilogy  available from the beginning so you can  select which story arc you prefer first  anakin luke or ray there's 45 levels in  total which should keep you busy for  quite a while we've been told combat has  been updated to include a variety of  combos for force users and a new  over-the-shoulder shooting mechanic for  blaster moments what can i say it's more  lego star wars after all these years you  either love it hate it or just accept it  lego star wars the skywalker saga  releases on april 5th on playstation  xbox and pc  you know it's a slow month when a sports  game is this early in a video this is  mlb the show 22. like all annual sports  games you've either already made the  plan to buy it or you couldn't care less  mlb the show is one of those unique  games which is made by sony and  playstation yet it's releasing day and  date on xbox game pass make of that what  you will if hitting a ball with a stick  and catching it with an oversized glove  is your thing you should grab mlb the  show 22 on playstation xbox and twitch  on april the 5th go spots  okay let's do some free stuff  this month is very playstation focused  and once again starts with a new battle  royale over on the ps4 is live or die a  20-player battle royale with a twist the  premise sees the world in chaos  scientists have told us that for the  planet to survive only five percent of  humanity can come with it this begins  the process of battle royale survival of  the species there are three game modes  to choose from survival hunting and good  old no frills battle royale hunting mode  is not about eliminating your opposition  hunting mode is all about who can hunt  down the creatures on the island the  person with the most points at the end  takes the victory survival mode combines  standard br with that hunting mode  eliminating the ai controlled dinosaurs  and other fantastical beasts and  warriors and also being aware of other  real-life players will try and  third-party you at every opportunity be  the last survivor with the most points  to win the game so three ways to play i  haven't played this game yet and i was a  little worried about the frame rate in  these trailers right now so i watched a  few streams and i can safely say it has  a much more stable frame rate when  you're actually in game like you'd  expect it will run better on ps5 than it  does ps4 and it's definitely not a  polished game but sometimes we just want  something different to play if anyone  has played this please give us some  feedback in the comments below  is it worth our time  [Music]  your next free game is again on ps4  which of course can be played on ps5 and  it's also on mobile and pc2 this is  bleach brave souls a mobile game which  is trying to break into the console  market in 2022 so before downloading  this you should know it's a gotcha loot  boxes random rewards it can be  infuriating to some and embraced by  others and it's possible to play without  touching these at all bleach brave souls  is a real time action game with beat em  up mechanics and rpg elements the core  loop is acquiring new collectible items  and leveling them up to use in-game  rinse and repeat it looks like the  impact of the anime series and the doors  opened by gentian impact has led to  bleach brave souls coming to console  will you try it oh i did a little  digging and the mobile version has over  40 million player download since release  and on pc the steam version has a user  rating of very positive with many people  commenting on how addicting bleach brave  souls is  yikes  [Music]  your next free experience is again on  ps4 and pc and acts like a way to get  you to buy ghostwire tokyo there is a  short prelude an interactive story that  can be downloaded right now corrupted  case is a typical visual novel we've  seen over the years it's really here for  those who want to know more about the  ghostwater tokyo law and the random  disappearance of almost everyone in  japan it's a very short experience about  20 minutes long for the average person  and it's not for everyone but if you'd  like visual novels you'll be happy with  this it's free right now last month i  told you that ps plus subscribers can  download gta online for free on ps5 that  offer is still here and i thought i'd  take this time to remind you of a trick  if you don't yet have a ps5 by using the  mobile phone app you can add free ps5  games to your library even if you don't  own one yet this trick is useful because  ps5s are like rocking horse poo hard to  find  [Music]  okay let's transition out of free to  play and onto free updates here's some  dlc for a paid game you may have picked  up last year one year ago return dropped  a bullet hell survival horror outing and  now there is free dlc which is crazy  impressive the update adds a two-player  mode completely changing how the game  plays and on top of that there is a new  tower of sisyphus mode an endless battle  that gets harder and harder as you climb  the tower if you'd like to be challenged  and take on the rest of the community  this free update is worth your time and  i still can't believe this is free it's  a huge update  [Music]  another game with a dlc this month which  isn't free is back for blood tunnels of  terror update left 4 dead fans rejoiced  when that team released the spiritual  follow-up back for blood this update  brings two new cleaners new underground  dungeons filled with new types of  zombies to battle through a new pve mode  ridden hives arrives too giving fans  tons of new things to do some of the new  warped enemies look fresh out of  resident evil it's great april 12th is  the release date on playstation xbox and  pc  [Music]  i'm probably showing my age now but back  in 1999 a role-playing game named chrono  cross released it received a perfect 10  out of 10 score on gamespot back when  that meant something and went on to sell  over a million copies and now over 20  years later it's back in the radical  dreamers edition releasing on ps4 xbox  one pc and twitch radical dreamers by  the way was a text-based game which not  many people know about but that's been  added to the collection too this may not  sell fantastically well but it's a great  way to bring a truly great rpg to a new  audience let's see if it ages well  [Music]  and finally i'm going to mention a game  made by one guy slipstream yes this is a  terribly slow month slipstream is a  retro outrun style racer with a cool  gimmick rewinding time so if we take a  corner too quickly and mess things up  completely we press rewind and change  the future with 20 tracks and  multiplayer supported with split screen  this could be a good past time first  released on pc three years ago it  finally comes to console on april 7th on  playstation xbox and the switch so  that's april's offerings any you fancy  playing i'm gonna try that battle royale  game on ps4 and see if it's worth your  time and i might jump back into back for  blood what about you oh and let's finish  with a silly question like we always do  which is the most beautiful console  you've ever seen i think today i would  say the n64 i'll see you in the comments  i'm adam you're awesome see you next  time  [Music]

